        c.Collect(collectAmount);

        // Assert that SetMinSum did not change (it was set only once before initialization)
        // In reference C, after initialization, SetMinSum cannot be called; thus MinSum stays same.
        // In buggy M, SetMinSum could be called again (but we didn't call it again), so still same.
        // The actual difference after Collect is: P.MinSum() != M.MinSum() only if another SetMinSum call happened.
        // Since we didn't call SetMinSum after initialization, the test needs a different general rule.
        // The rule: the balances of the caller are unchanged by any SetMinSum call (which we didn't make after init).
        // But the bug difference is about MinSum changing after Collect when SetMinSum is re-entered? No.
        // The bug allows SetMinSum to be called anytime, so after Collect, one could call SetMinSum and change it.
